    sha256: 0cf245521764b405f4d8983f1b93f131dbe6d9cacd000a0ed9edeb1aca4f9b0b
  body: "# Understandable prior information and notification evidence\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\n\
    The captured guidance requires clear prior information about specified responsibilities and sanction
    consequences, considers the claimant’s ability to understand and make representations, and requires
    evidence of adequate notification.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThe quality and accessibility of
    information matter alongside delivery. DMG 34033 and 34038 continue onto neighbouring pages; the source
    gives different notification routes and specific scheme requirements. Retrievable notification evidence
    is not a requirement that the decision maker routinely inspect every notice. This does not prescribe
    one universal notification format or determine the validity of a real sanction.\n\n## Inspected source
    passages\n\n- [DMG 34033, PDF page 8](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/628f5e0bd3bf7f0373c74ef9/dmgch34.pdf#page=8)
    — DMG Vol 6 Ch 34: Sanctions.\n- [DMG 34034, PDF page 9](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/628f5e0bd3bf7f0373c74ef9/dmgch34.pdf#page=9)
    — DMG Vol 6 Ch 34: Sanctions.\n- [DMG 34035, PDF page 9](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/628f5e0bd3bf7f0373c74ef9/dmgch34.pdf#page=9)
    — DMG Vol 6 Ch 34: Sanctions.\n- [DMG 34038, PDF page 10](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/628f5e0bd3bf7f0373c74ef9/dmgch34.pdf#page=10)
    — DMG Vol 6 Ch 34: Sanctions.\n- [Inspected continuation, PDF page 9](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/628f5e0bd3bf7f0373c74ef9/dmgch34.pdf#page=9)
    — context for the selected paragraph.\n- [Inspected continuation, PDF page 11](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/628f5e0bd3bf7f0373c74ef9/dmgch34.pdf#page=11)
    — context for the selected paragraph.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted interpretation
    of selected passages in the 15 September 2026 frozen source snapshot. Specialist review is required.
    Source acquisition, source revision, legal effective dates and this record’s authoring time are separate.\n\
    \nThis is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, individual advice,
    an entitlement decision or an executable rule. Machine-extracted text may alter reading order, footnotes
    and characters. No PDF visual inspection, whole-chapter coverage or behavioural evaluation pass is
    claimed by this record.\n\n- `dmg-vol6-ch34`: PDF SHA-256 `0cf245521764b405f4d8983f1b93f131dbe6d9cacd000a0ed9edeb1aca4f9b0b`;
    extracted pages SHA-256 `b33b6233590a7183795624a56525dfb2594dae0d201c5d33b36ff7ec8a3c74ce`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/dmg-evidence-assessment
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The notification passage requires the department to be able to produce evidence that
      the claimant was adequately informed, with the particular requirements depending on context.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol6-ch34/0010
      quote: "34038 Notifications form an integral part of any appeal submission to demonstrate that the
        department\nwas legally compliant with the ‘prior information requirement’ and have to be available
        if requested by\nthe judiciary. Therefore whatever is required of a claimant in their responsibilities,
        the Secretary of State\nhas to be able to produce evidence to support that the claimant was adequately
        informed if a sanction is\nto be imposed. This can be a copy of a formal written notification
        or a screen print of system records\nshowing records of a telephone conversation, face to face
        interview, text or email message. For\nguidance on specific notification requirements in certain
        circumstances see further guidance at\n\n\n1. DMG 34723 regarding informing the claimant of a
        job vacancy\n\n\n2. DMG 34765 regarding mandating a claimant to the MWA scheme\n\n\n3. DMG 34866
        regarding mandating a claimant to a SAPOE (‘work for your benefit’) scheme\n\n\n4. DMG 34901 et
        seq regarding issuing a JSD.\n\n\nNote 1: The DM should be mindful of the ‘prior information requirement’
        whenever the Secretary of State\nrequires the claimant to take part in an action or activity which
        could result in a sanction to benefit.\n\n\nNote 2: It is not essential that the DM routinely
        sees a copy of every notification in order to be able to"
      locator: DMG 34038
  - target: term/legacy-jsa-good-reason
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: Information and an opportunity for representations are distinct from the later
      good-reason enquiry, which itself has exceptions.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol6-ch34/0008
      quote: "34033 The ‘prior information requirement’ principle is from a judgement of the Court of
        Appeal 1. The\njudgement provided, in the general interest of fairness,\n\n\n1.   each claimant’s
        responsibilities and\n\n\n2. the consequences of not meeting them\n\n\nshould be set out clearly
        in understandable terms at the stage of specification of particular actions or\nactivities so
        that claimants can make informed and meaningful representations at the relevant time.\n\n\nNote
        1: The ‘prior information requirement’ may therefore be relevant both to whether the claimant
        has\nbeen validly referred to a specific requirement and also to whether there was good reason
        for not\ncomplying with it."
      locator: DMG 34033
    - page: page/dmg-vol6-ch34/0058
      quote: "34201 For JSA intermediate sanctions there is no ‘good reason’ for the DM to consider before
        imposing\n\na reduction1. The DM is considering whether entitlement has ended on a previous occasion
        due to the\nclaimant not being available and/or ASE (see guidance at DMG 34121 et seq).\n\n\n\
        \                                                                                          1 JS
        Act 95, s 19B"
      locator: DMG 34201
    - page: page/dmg-vol6-ch34/0058
      quote: "34202 For sanctionable failures due to misconduct the claimant will not have an opportunity
        to show\ngood reason for the failure but will be given the opportunity to provide facts and evidence
        for\nconsideration by the DM (see guidance on Misconduct at DMG 34531).\n\n\n\n\nMeaning of good
        reason"
      locator: DMG 34202
